<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.paleo.heavymetalindex.daemon</string>

  <!--
    Invocation note (2026-05-14): launchd is configured to invoke /bin/bash
    directly with the script path as its first argument. The previous form
    (bash -lc "<path>") relied on bash to exec the script, which macOS blocks
    when the script carries a com.apple.provenance xattr (set on any file
    written by a sandboxed process like Claude Code). The current form
    reads the script and interprets it without exec'ing the file, bypassing
    the provenance check.

    If you still see "Operation not permitted" in /tmp/heavymetalindex-daemon.err.log:
      sudo xattr -cr ~/Desktop/heavy-metal-index/tools/autonomy/
      launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.paleo.heavymetalindex.daemon
      cp tools/autonomy/com.paleo.heavymetalindex.daemon.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.paleo.heavymetalindex.daemon.plist
  -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/karenpendergrass/Desktop/heavy-metal-index/tools/autonomy/daemon-tick.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!--
    2026-05-30 — KEYSTONE RELIABILITY FIX (Opus 4.8). Replaced
    StartCalendarInterval (:00/:30, no KeepAlive) with KeepAlive=true.

    WHY. The :00/:30 calendar schedule kept WEDGING. After a tick exited
    non-zero (git fatal=128, an unguarded grep, an empty-glob under the old
    set -e), launchd recorded last-exit=128 and silently STOPPED firing the
    calendar events. `launchctl print` showed runs=17 total over five days
    and state=not-running, while caffeinate (PreventUserIdleSystemSleep) was
    holding the Mac awake and pmset read sleep=0 — so this was NOT sleep. The
    only ticks that happened were humans/threads hand-kickstarting at odd
    minutes. Net result: ~12 papers ingested in 48h on a system meant to
    self-build hundreds/day. Documented multi-hour silent deaths: 05-26
    (~16h), 05-29 (~13h), 05-29→30 (~6.5h).

    THE PRIMITIVE THAT ACTUALLY SURVIVES HERE. The sibling job
    com.paleo.heavymetalindex.awake uses KeepAlive=true and has stayed up
    continuously in this exact launchd domain while THIS job's calendar
    schedule died. KeepAlive=true means "if the process is not running,
    (re)start it" — it fires on EVERY exit path: clean exit, crash, signal,
    non-zero status. There is no wedged state. A single bad tick can no
    longer take the scheduler down for 13 hours; launchd brings it right
    back. This is strictly stronger than StartCalendarInterval, which only
    fires on a wall-clock edge and gives up after a bad exit.

    CADENCE. daemon-tick.sh is one bounded unit of work: it runs the
    deterministic phase + fetch + a capped ingest batch (HMI_MFETCH_MAX_PDFS,
    concurrency HMI_MFETCH_CONCURRENCY), commits, pushes, exits. KeepAlive
    then reruns it. ThrottleInterval=1800 is the floor BETWEEN starts:
      - Busy tick (ingesting a batch, ~30-60 min) exits after >1800s, so the
        next tick starts immediately → continuous queue drain while there is
        fuel.
      - Idle tick (no fresh PDFs, exits in ~70s) → launchd waits out the
        1800s floor → a fresh tick every ~30 min to pick up newly-fetched
        PDFs and regenerate deterministic artifacts. Same 30-min idle pulse
        the old :00/:30 schedule intended, but now un-wedgeable.

    PAUSE. The ~/.heavymetalindex.STOP halt file still works: with it
    present each tick exits 0 in <1s and KeepAlive just idle-spins every
    ThrottleInterval doing nothing. To fully stop: bootout the job.

    The PID lock + commit-lock + EXIT-trap recovery inside daemon-tick.sh
    (added by parallel sessions 05-28→30) handle overlap and dirty-tree
    recovery; this plist guarantees the loop is always running to begin with.
  -->
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>1800</integer>

  <!-- Start the loop immediately on load and on every login/reboot. With
       KeepAlive this is what makes the system self-start after a power
       cycle without anyone kickstarting it. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/heavymetalindex-daemon.out.log</string>

  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/heavymetalindex-daemon.err.log</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HMI_REPO_ROOT</key>
    <string>/Users/karenpendergrass/Desktop/heavy-metal-index</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
